<p>NOTE: (A) Non-recurring $32 million gain ($19 million after tax or $.07 per share) from June 1997 sale of certain domestic regional brands and non-recurring domestic expenses of $31 million ($18 million after tax or $.07 per share). Non-recurring domestic expenses include $14 million provision for an additional write-down of a business held for sale; $10 million expense for the reorganization of the U.S. Foods Group selling organization; and $7 million expense for relocating International headquarters to New Jersey.</p>
<p>(B) Non-recurring domestic expenses associated with the implementation of June 1996 restructuring program ($6 million after tax or $.02 per share).</p>
<p>(C) June 1996 restructuring expense of $428 million ($300 million after tax or $1.13 per share) related to the domestic and international businesses of $353 million and $75 million, respectively.</p>
